---
title: TikFinity setup
pageSlug: tikfinity-setup
mod: tikfinitok
section: config
order: 2
---

In TikFinity: **Setup → Minecraft Connection**.

- Host: `127.0.0.1`
- Port: `4567`

The username field must match your in-game name exactly. `Steve` and `steve` are different.

Make an action that uses **Exec Minecraft Command**. A gift that drops a zombie above you:

```
execute at YourName run summon zombie ~ ~5 ~
```

A rose that gives a golden apple:

```
execute as YourName run give @s golden_apple
```

Keep commands cheap at first. A raid every like will ruin a recording faster than it will make a clip.

After the first launch you can change the port in `config/tikfinitok-common.toml`. Anything that talks ServerTap HTTP can use that same API. TikFinity is just the common client.
